NNAAMMEE
     veldxf - convert between DXF and vellum drawings

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     vveellddxxff [-llaayyeerr _n_a_m_e=_n] [-ssccaallee _N] _f_i_l_e._d_x_f > _f_i_l_e._d
     vveellddxxff -xx _f_i_l_e._d ... > _f_i_l_e._d_x_f

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     vveellddxxff is the border with the office CAD, and it crosses in
     both directions.  Read a DXF file (the R10-era plain-text
     format) and it prints an ordinary vveelllluumm drawing on standard
     output; give it -xx and it reads drawings and prints a DXF
     ENTITIES section instead.  The two directions are one
     program because they are one format, and because the pair
     has to FIX-POINT: a drawing exported and re-imported is the
     same drawing, and the shipped regression gate proves it on
     every run.

     Conversion is not a link.  Run it once; the result is a
     drawing like any other, and nothing remembers where it came
     from.

IIMMPPOORRTT
     The scope is the honest entity subset:

                        LINEa vellum L line
                        CIRCLEa C circle
                        ARCan A arc (centre, radius and angles land exactly)
                        TEXTa T label at the nearest of the three sizes
                        POLYLINEa P polyline (LWPOLYLINE too; split at the
                                  20-point ceiling)

     Everything else is SKIPPED AND COUNTED: the run ends with a
     report like ``dropped: 12 SPLINE, 3 INSERT'' on the diagnos-
     tic output, because a silent partial import is how drawings
     lose limbs.  Flatten blocks at the source; a SPLINE can be
     chorded by whatever exported it.

     DXF layer names fold onto vellum's four layers through the
     -llaayyeerr map; a bare digit name (``0''..``3'') folds onto it-
     self and anything unmapped lands on layer 0.  -ssccaallee gives
     the number of drawing units in one grid unit - the default 1
     takes one unit as one millimetre - and the matching UU units
     header is emitted.  Coordinates may carry decimals; they are
     handled in fixed point (no floating point anywhere).  The
     drawing's minimum corner lands at grid 0,0 with the y axis
     flipped (DXF y runs up).

EEXXPPOORRTT
     -xx writes the sheets named after it into ONE ENTITIES sec-
     tion on standard output, the way a set prints onto one roll.
     Coordinates are in GRID units at a pinned quarter-unit
     resolution, so symbol geometry emits exactly as .25 steps; y
     is flipped (DXF y runs up); arcs are true ARC entities, not
     chords, because a chorded arc is correct on paper and wrong


